{#
	Contact: the booking form. It's a real Total CMS form, so each message is
	saved in the Enquiries collection and shows in the admin. If email is set up,
	it's sent to you as well.

	Three settings make a form safe to put on a public page:
	  addOnly        visitors can only create, never edit, an enquiry
	  botProtection  a honeypot and a time trap that turn away simple spam bots
	  publicOperations  set to "create" on the Enquiries collection in its settings

	newActions says what happens after sending: first the "new-enquiry" email (the
	template is in the Mailer collection), then the thank-you message. "continue"
	means a mail problem doesn't lose the visitor's message.

	The Sessions and Prints pages link here with ?interest=Golden%20Hour. Anything
	after the ? arrives as getData, and "default" puts it in the field.
#}
{% extends 'layouts/default.twig' %}

{% block content %}
	{% include 'partials/band.twig' with {title: page.title, intro: page.data.intro|default('')} %}

	<section class="sheet section grid" data-tracks="12" data-threshold="md" data-gap="lg">
		<div class="stack" data-span="4" data-gap="sm">
			<h2>Write to me</h2>
			<p>{{ info.responseTime }}</p>
			<p><a href="mailto:{{ info.email }}">{{ info.email }}</a></p>
			{% if info.phone %}<p>{{ info.phone }}</p>{% endif %}
			<p class="muted">{{ info.base }}</p>
		</div>

		<div data-span="7" data-start="6">
			{% set form = cms.form.builder('enquiries', {
				addOnly: true,
				botProtection: true,
				save: 'Send',
				fieldIcons: false,
				newActions: [
					{action: 'mailer', mailerId: 'new-enquiry', continue: true},
					{action: 'message', text: 'Thank you. Your note is on its way, and I will write back soon.'}
				]
			}) %}
			{% do form.addField('name') %}
			{% do form.addField('email') %}
			{% do form.addField('phone') %}
			{% do form.addField('topic', {default: getData.topic|default('') == 'print' ? 'A print' : 'A portrait session'}) %}
			{% do form.addField('interest', {default: getData.interest|default('')}) %}
			{% do form.addField('preferredDate') %}
			{% do form.addField('place') %}
			{% do form.addField('message', {field: 'textarea'}) %}
			{{ form.build() }}
		</div>
	</section>
{% endblock %}
